WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:08.530
OK, there was a complete total softball, pandering
brownnosing interview that Donald Trump did

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:12.160
on Fox News with Sean Hannity on Thursday
night.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.460
Let's look at some clips will jump right into
it.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:19.440
The sort of framework here was Donald Trump
doing a media tour because of the death of

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.619
radical right wing radio host Rush Limbaugh?

00:00:21.619 --> 00:00:28.650
Reminder, Rush Limbaugh celebrated the death
of Ruth Bader Ginsburg, celebrated the deaths

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:31.010
of AIDS victims in the 90s.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:32.439
Not a good guy.

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:33.439
Trump calling in.

00:00:33.439 --> 00:00:38.460
And Hannity starts in with, you know, Mr.
President, sir, it was such a great idea to

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.769
give Rush Limbaugh the Presidential Medal
of Freedom.

00:00:40.769 --> 00:00:43.539
How did you come up with such a great idea?

00:00:43.539 --> 00:00:44.539
Total suck up.

00:00:44.539 --> 00:00:45.539
Let's take a listen.

00:00:45.539 --> 00:00:46.539
A true original.

00:00:46.539 --> 00:00:49.989
Joining us now on the phone is President Donald
Trump.

00:00:49.989 --> 00:00:56.579
Mr. President, I know that the honor of his
life came from you.

00:00:56.579 --> 00:01:02.420
And what that Medal of Freedom meant to him,
I know the behind the scenes story, I know

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:08.520
I know who made the first call to me anyway
was Matt Drudge and and Jared Kushner.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:14.710
And and I know you made your decision and
with Melania there in about five seconds and

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:16.840
you said that's a great idea.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:17.840
Tell us about it.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:24.580
Well, it was an idea that we had that a lot
of people suggested to me, frankly, a lot

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.609
of great people of our country, largely Republicans.

00:01:28.609 --> 00:01:33.479
It was an amazing night because the Republicans
went wild and the Democrats sat there.

00:01:33.479 --> 00:01:36.369
But they all respected Rush.

00:01:36.369 --> 00:01:40.720
And I think it was, you know, one of the great
honors of his life, Presidential Medal of

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:41.909
Freedom.

00:01:41.909 --> 00:01:43.070
It's a big deal.

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:46.540
And he he was very honored by it.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:49.369
And he was a great gentleman, just like Mark
said.

00:01:49.369 --> 00:01:52.729
I listened to Mark and Mark is so terrific.

00:01:52.729 --> 00:01:56.619
But, you know, he said he's special and Rush
was really special.

00:01:56.619 --> 00:01:58.090
He was a very special guy.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:00.299
And you said irreplaceable.

00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:01.299
And it's true.

00:02:01.299 --> 00:02:02.299
He is irreplaceable.

00:02:02.299 --> 00:02:10.759
Again, Trump deciding that the thing he gave
Rush was the thing Rush was the most honored

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:11.759
by.

00:02:11.759 --> 00:02:15.930
Trump needs that to be true for his own narcissism.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:22.209
And he keeps repeating that the right loves
Rush and the left respected Rush.

00:02:22.209 --> 00:02:25.849
I don't know anyone on the left that respected
Rush Limbaugh.

00:02:25.849 --> 00:02:29.930
I don't know anyone on the left who would
have respect for people who celebrate the

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:34.239
deaths of people with AIDS or celebrate the
death of Ruth Bader Ginsburg.

00:02:34.239 --> 00:02:37.890
These aren't mere political differences about
what the tax rate should be, where you say,

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.930
hey, you know what, we disagree, but I respect
their point of view.

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:44.690
Cheering AIDS deaths has nothing respectable
about it.

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:48.220
It is a bizarre thing for Donald Trump to
keep repeating.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:52.269
Then Hannity goes into even more sucking up
to Trump.

00:02:52.269 --> 00:02:57.720
And Trump again reveals that the thing he
really likes about Rush is that he supported

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:58.720
Trump.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:02:59.720
That's all Trump cares about.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:05.189
You know, there's this side of you that I
know a lot of Americans don't know and I know

00:03:05.189 --> 00:03:08.970
many people that this story holds true for.

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:16.900
And I know in the case of Rush and when Rush
had his diagnosis a little over a year ago,

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:23.349
I knew you were calling him regularly, minimum
of once a month, often much more than that.

00:03:23.349 --> 00:03:25.480
And you would always be checking with how
are you feeling?

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:28.799
How are the treatments, how's everything going?

00:03:28.799 --> 00:03:30.990
And and I know you talked to him a lot.

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:32.819
What were those conversations like?

00:03:32.819 --> 00:03:37.590
Well, it was interesting because I didn't
know Rush at all, as you know, I didn't know

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:44.230
him at all until I had gotten word that from
somebody that Russia was with us all the way.

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:49.050
He was you know, we have this guy who was
so big on radio.

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:52.310
I knew a lot about Russia, but I didn't know
him.

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:53.750
And he was with me all the way.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.110
And it was sort of incredible.

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:57.629
I got to know him after that.

00:03:57.629 --> 00:04:00.150
And he was much different, actually.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:07.769
You know, when you were there was a very,
very I wouldn't say not outgoing, but he was

00:04:07.769 --> 00:04:11.989
very, very warm and he was just a very warm
person.

00:04:11.989 --> 00:04:16.130
And and, you know, when people got to know
him, I loved playing golf with Russian as

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:20.540
I used to call on the bull because he was
actually a very strong guy, physically very

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:21.540
strong guy.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:24.690
And he hit the ball a long way when he hit
it big, went a long way.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:27.310
And but you got to know him.

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:30.940
And he and he loved this country and he loved
his wife.

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:37.270
All the things Trump says about Rush, his
ratings, his ability to do a radio show, all

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:42.450
that stuff, it would all be equally true even
if Russia didn't support Trump.

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:48.560
But you and I know that if Rush was an anti
Trump Republican who died, Donald Trump would

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:49.570
not be doing this.

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:51.270
Donald Trump doesn't have friends.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:55.110
The only thing that matters to Trump is, are
you a brownnosing sycophant?

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:58.900
If so, I'll call you a friend until you say
the wrong thing.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:04.640
And then I say you're, you know, what's that
lightweight as he often says, what you do,

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:09.300
what you do for me and what you've done lately
is all that matters to Donald Trump.

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:10.850
Let's look at a little bit more of this.

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:16.330
Here is Sean Hannity with just a stunning
brownnosing of Trump saying, hey, here were

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:18.380
Russia's top issues.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.850
These are your issues as well, sir.

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:23.300
Mr. President Trump on Russia's show today.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:30.240
And I was listening for I began my radio program
and they played a segment of Rush.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:35.210
And in that segment, he said if you took tapes
of him when he started in nineteen eighty

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:39.010
eight and syndication again, nobody thought
that that anyone can syndicate during the

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:41.350
daytime and be successful.

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:44.600
And he proved all the naysayers wrong.

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:52.280
And if you look at where he stood, conservative
justices, liberty, freedom, less government

00:05:52.280 --> 00:06:00.420
intrusion, intrusion, less regulation, less
taxes, lower taxes, energy independence, secure

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:04.060
borders, choice and schools.

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:05.390
The Second Amendment.

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:06.900
Free and fair trade.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:09.160
Peace through strength.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:10.250
Sound familiar?

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:11.520
Because that's your agenda.

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:12.520
That's what you did.

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:14.220
He was right there.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:15.220
He understood it.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:16.220
He got it.

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:17.220
And he's been that way for a long time.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:19.290
You know, he hasn't been somebody that's changed.

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:22.310
He didn't go from being a liberal to being
a conservative.

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:28.320
I mean, he was there from the beginning and
he hasn't changed his views and changed very

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:29.490
much.

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:34.350
And his audiences, you know better than probably
anybody in the loyalty of his audience was

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:35.550
just incredible, staggering.

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:40.270
It's actually interesting and sad how never
changing your views is seen as a badge of

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:43.680
honor in some circles on the right and on
the left.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:49.730
And as I've said many times, having the exact
same views for fifty years likely means you're

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:50.760
not learning anything.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:52.170
Now, I want to be really clear.

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:57.730
I don't mean it's typical for, say, a 40 year
old not talking about anyone in particular

00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:03.210
for a forty year old to have a complete political
awakening and and 180 degree reversal where

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:07.270
all of a sudden they denounce everything they
stood for for forty years and say, I was wrong

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:09.620
all along and I'm actually a right wing nut.

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:14.240
OK, that raises red flags and it suggests
to me grifting.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:18.990
But what I'm talking about is saying your
views haven't changed at all for forty, fifty

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:21.450
years, as if it's a badge of honor.

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:26.530
Look at how much we've learned about life
and humanity and the planet in 50 years.

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:30.070
How could your views not change over that
period of time?

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:35.790
Even my views on many issues are modified
and adjusted and updated to account for new

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:37.480
things that we know.

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:42.890
It's sad and it doesn't bode well for the
country to see that praised as a badge of

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:43.890
honor.

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:44.890
Just one more clip here.

00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:48.150
Hannity explaining what might have been so
damaging to Kayleigh McEnany.

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:49.200
Listen to this.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:53.190
Your own Kayleigh McEnany, I mentioned earlier
